Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arrayWeights(): fix the convergence criterion of the
 prior-weights REML fit

.arrayWeightsPrWtsREML() (src/awreml.c) divided the Fisher-scoring
convergence criterion by (ngenes+prior.n) a second time: the score
vector and information matrix are already per-gene averages, so the
criterion was (ngenes+prior.n) times smaller than the one used by
.arrayWeightsREML() for the same state, and the default tol=1e-5 was
met after one or two iterations. With a weight matrix of ones the two
routines fit the same model but returned weights differing by up to
15% (10,000 genes, 8 arrays). The criterion is now num/ngam, the same
per-gene scale as .arrayWeightsREML(), so the two routines agree to
rounding on equal prior weights.

Adds tests/arrayweights-reml.R and changelog/NEWS entries.

